course: dictionary
lesson: 13347
title: Hairless: a word with a clue inside
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are built from smaller parts, and the parts give you clues. Hairless is made of hair and -less. The ending -less means without, so hairless means without hair. «The hairless cat sat in the sunshine.» This cat has no fur at all.
explain: Other -less words work the same way. Careless means without care, and harmless means without harm. Check your clue in a sentence: «The baby mouse was hairless and pink.» Does without hair make sense there? Yes, so your meaning fits.
explain: Hairless does not always mean totally bare. Dolphins are almost hairless, so the word can mean having very little hair, not only none at all. Read the whole sentence to decide which one the writer means.
fact: «Hairless» means having no hair or very little hair.
fact: The ending -less means without, so hair + less = hairless.
fact: Naked mole rats and dolphins are almost hairless.
fact: The Sphynx is a hairless breed of cat.
fact: Many newborn mice are born hairless.
exercise: «The Sphynx is a hairless breed of cat.» What does hairless mean? | Covered in feathers | Having very long, thick fur | *Having no hair or very little hair | Able to fly high in the sky
exercise: Which part of hairless means without? | *-less | hairl | hair | -ful
exercise: «The baby mouse was hairless and pink.» What does hairless mean here? | Covered in thick fur | Painted pink | *Without hair | Very tall
test: «Dolphins are almost hairless.» What does almost hairless mean here? | Having no skin at all | Having a thick, warm coat | *Having very little hair | Able to swim very fast
test: What does the ending -less tell you in hairless? | It means again and again | It means full of hair | It means very hairy | *It means without, so the word means without hair
exam: Jayden reads «The hairless character was an alien.» What does hairless mean? | Having a long beard | Flying high above the trees | *Having no hair or very little hair | Having a lot of hair
